Qt runtime in Puls

This distribution includes dynamically linked Qt @Qt6_VERSION@ libraries and
plugins deployed by the official Qt CMake deployment API. The unmodified Qt
license texts are in the Qt/ directory. Additional notices supplied by the build
SDK, when available, are preserved in Qt/sdk/.

Qt is developed by The Qt Company and the Qt community. Qt's licensing information
and source code are available from the official project:
https://www.qt.io/licensing/open-source-lgpl-obligations
https://code.qt.io/cgit/qt/
https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/

Qt license texts included by Puls are copied without modification from the Qt
SDK's LICENSES files. Their original names identify their SPDX license variants.
They are notices for Qt; the Puls application license is in the adjacent LICENSE.

On Linux, the C library, ELF loader, graphics drivers, system fonts and CA trust
store are provided by the target operating system.
